      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.196,
          "end": 5.196,
          "en": "So now after lots of important theory,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 6,
          "end": 10.11,
          "en": "I want to get back to working on that input form here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 10.11,
          "end": 13.5,
          "en": "And I wanna make sure that we now actually do use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 13.5,
          "end": 16.65,
          "en": "the submitted values to create a new ticket.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 16.65,
          "end": 19.89,
          "en": "And of course, I wanna make sure that we then also show",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 19.89,
          "end": 22.143,
          "en": "those tickets on the screen eventually.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 23.64,
          "end": 26.73,
          "en": "Now, for handling those tickets,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 26.73,
          "end": 29.443,
          "en": "we now got different options.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 29.443,
          "end": 33.12,
          "en": "We could use a tickets service,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 33.12,
          "end": 35.4,
          "en": "which we use for storing the tickets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.4,
          "end": 38.97,
          "en": "and for providing those tickets.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.97,
          "end": 43.26,
          "en": "But alternatively, we could also manage them in a property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 43.26,
          "end": 47.34,
          "en": "of the tickets component and use a custom event,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 47.34,
          "end": 49.86,
          "en": "an output to pass the submitted data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 49.86,
          "end": 53.8,
          "en": "from the new ticket component to the tickets component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 53.8,
          "end": 58.59,
          "en": "and then update that tickets data here in that component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 58.59,
          "end": 61.47,
          "en": "whenever new data is submitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 61.47,
          "end": 64.41,
          "en": "And that's the approach I'll use here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 64.41,
          "end": 67.35,
          "en": "though you could absolutely also use a service,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 67.35,
          "end": 70.89,
          "en": "but since this section here is about diving deeper",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 70.89,
          "end": 74.85,
          "en": "into components, I'll use that component focused approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 74.85,
          "end": 76.383,
          "en": "instead of a service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 78,
          "end": 81.6,
          "en": "And therefore here, I'll add a tickets property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 81.6,
          "end": 83.82300000000001,
          "en": "to the tickets component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 84.9,
          "end": 87.99,
          "en": "And that should hold an array of tickets.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 87.99,
          "end": 90.39,
          "en": "And initially it might be an empty array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 90.39,
          "end": 95.39,
          "en": "but of course I wanted to find the shape of every ticket.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 95.88,
          "end": 100.483,
          "en": "And therefore I'll add a ticket.model dot TypeScript file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 100.483,
          "end": 104.82,
          "en": "where I will export a ticket interface",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 104.82,
          "end": 109.12299999999999,
          "en": "that describes that shape of such a ticket.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 109.12299999999999,
          "end": 112.86,
          "en": "And here I'll keep it fairly simple.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 112.86,
          "end": 117.03,
          "en": "Every ticket should have an ID, of type string, let's say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 117.03,
          "end": 119.944,
          "en": "could also be a number, but here I'll go for a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 119.944,
          "end": 123.57,
          "en": "It should have a title, which is a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 123.57,
          "end": 127.123,
          "en": "And then the the request text of that ticket,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 127.123,
          "end": 131.25,
          "en": "which is a string, and a status.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 131.25,
          "end": 133.08,
          "en": "And for the status,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 133.08,
          "end": 136.68,
          "en": "I want to allow two possible string values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 136.68,
          "end": 140.763,
          "en": "I wanna allow open and closed like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 142.23,
          "end": 145.871,
          "en": "So I have this union type of these two string literal types",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 145.871,
          "end": 148.89,
          "en": "as they're called.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 148.89,
          "end": 150.73,
          "en": "It's the same approach as before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 151.992,
          "end": 153.083,
          "en": "in the server status component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 153.942,
          "end": 156.27,
          "en": "where we also allowed multiple string values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 156.27,
          "end": 157.893,
          "en": "as alternative values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 158.74099999999999,
          "end": 160.92000000000002,
          "en": "but where we wanted specific string values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 160.92000000000002,
          "end": 162.513,
          "en": "as allowed values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 163.38,
          "end": 165.603,
          "en": "So that's now the ticket model.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 167.941,
          "end": 171.69,
          "en": "In the tickets component, I then can tell TypeScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 171.69,
          "end": 175.74,
          "en": "that tickets will be an array of such tickets.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 175.74,
          "end": 180.74,
          "en": "So I'm importing tickets from ticket model file here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 181.83,
          "end": 183.52,
          "en": "And I then tell TypeScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 184.4,
          "end": 186.03,
          "en": "that tickets will be an array of such tickets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 186.03,
          "end": 189.12,
          "en": "by using this type definition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 189.12,
          "end": 192.24099999999999,
          "en": "You'll always add those square brackets after a type name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 192.24099999999999,
          "end": 196.98,
          "en": "to tell TypeScript that it'll be an array of that type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 196.98,
          "end": 200.043,
          "en": "an array of objects that have this ticket shape,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 200.88,
          "end": 202.14,
          "en": "or an empty array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 202.14,
          "end": 203.343,
          "en": "That's also fine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 204.21,
          "end": 208.2,
          "en": "Now of course, we must make sure that we can add tickets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 208.2,
          "end": 209.253,
          "en": "to this array.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
